      "title": "Add a defensive content scraper for thin sources",
      "number": 2,
      "goFurther": "🛠️ Break it on purpose: temporarily change the timeout in fetch_full_text() from 10 to 0.001 seconds and run the live Wikipedia check again. Confirm it still prints the SKIPPED line instead of crashing your terminal with a traceback - that's the try/except around requests.get() doing its job.",
      "description": "Some Tavily snippets are too short to cite meaningfully. This build fetches the full page for exactly those sources - and is built to never crash the whole research run over one blocked or broken site, since that happens constantly on the open web."
