      "title": "Build the synthesizer and the citation guard",
      "number": 3,
      "goFurther": "🛠️🛠️ In synthesize.py's self-test, add a THIRD fake reply where the AI cites the same invented source twice in one line, e.g. `- A claim [Source 5] backed up by [Source 5] again`. Confirm _strip_invented_citations() catches and marks BOTH occurrences, not just the first - that's what the regex substitution (not a single find-and-replace) buys you.",
      "description": "This is the heart of the project - turning a pile of sources into one structured, cited brief. It's also where this project makes its core safety promise real: the AI is never trusted to only cite real sources on its own word alone, so every citation gets checked in code before you ever read the output."
